Option Explicit


' =============================================================================
' PNL Explainer BiG - HEDGE LOAD
'
' This module does ONE job, and it is now the only macro the workbook needs:
' Load_Hedges.
'
' It reads the desk's two coverage books, works out what each hedge covers,
' writes the mapping columns of the Futures and Swaps sheets, and stamps the
' coverage links back onto Bonds!SwapLink / Bonds!FutLink.
'
' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
' THREE RULES
'
' 1) IT DOES NOT FORMAT ANYTHING.
'
'    No font, colour, alignment, column width, ClearFormats or NumberFormat
'    write remains, and none may be added.  The workbook's appearance is the
'    desk's, not the macro's.
'
'    This also used to be a stability problem, not just a taste one:
'    AppendSwapMapRowsToSwaps set NumberFormat = "@" across a quarter of a
'    million mostly-empty cells on every run, which pinned UsedRange at row
'    50,004 for ever and made each subsequent "clear" a 50,000-row operation.
'    Text-sensitive identifiers are written with a leading apostrophe instead
'    (see TextSafe), which costs nothing and touches no cell format.
'
' 2) IT DOES NOT WRITE HEADERS, AND IT DOES NOT WRITE FORMULAS.
'
'    Row 4 is CHECKED against the layout this module compiles against, and a
'    mismatch stops the run before anything is touched - see
'    AssertHedgeSheetHeaders.  Where the load adds rows past the end of an
'    existing formula block, FillFormulaColumnsDown replicates the formula the
'    column ALREADY has, in R1C1 form, onto the new rows only.  The macro never
'    authors a formula and never overwrites one.
'
' 3) IT WRITES ONLY THE COLUMNS IT OWNS.
'
'    FuturesOwnedColumns and SwapsOwnedColumns are the whole list.  Everything
'    else on those two sheets belongs to the formulas the desk put there.  The
'    previous build cleared and rewrote the full sheet width on every run,
'    which destroyed every BDP and BQL formula on Futures and Swaps - including
'    Swaps!O (DV01 BBG) and the entire BQL block, the numbers the attribution
'    is built on.
' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
'
' WHAT WAS FIXED IN THIS BUILD
'
' The column constants below had drifted from the sheets - by one column on
' Futures, one on the Bonds link columns, and TEN on Swaps after that sheet
' gained DV01 BBG plus a BQL block at O:X.  Seventy-three constants were wrong.
' Nothing errored; the load simply wrote to the wrong cells:
'
'   - Hedge_Source and Hedge_Class landed on Coverage_BPV and Link_Source, so
'     PNL_Attribution's filters on AM="RTJ" and AO="RATES" matched nothing and
'     every futures hedge summed to zero;
'   - the swap mapping block landed across O:AD, on top of live market data;
'   - Bonds!SwapLink landed on FutLink and FutLink on BBG_Cand_ISIN, corrupting
'     a bond pricing input.
'
' Futures!Hedge_Class and Swaps!FloatCurve_Type were also DECLARED and never
' written, which zeroed the futures hedge and silently zeroed the swap curve
' model independently of the shift above.
'
' The header assertion exists so that this class of failure can only ever
' produce a message, never a wrong number.
'
' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
'
' OPICS IS GONE.  The database was only ever asked for exchange, face value,
' delivery, CTD and average entry price for the futures, plus PayFixed for the
' swaps.  Four of those are already Bloomberg formulas on the Futures sheet;
' the other two are properties of the contract root and are now a table.  See
' "FUTURES CONTRACT SPECIFICATION".
'
' See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md for how the pieces fit and docs/COLUMNS.md for the
' sheet contracts.
' =============================================================================


